# Prebuilt dependency closures published as GitHub release assets, and the tag they live
# under. fetch.sh reads both from this file, so the tag and the hashes cannot drift apart.
#
# The asset is not content-addressed by its name: a moved tag or a re-uploaded file is the
# same URL. These hashes are what identify it, and fetch.sh will not unpack without them.
#
# To publish a new set:
#   1. nix build .#libcxx-deps-<triple>          -- or tools/deps/build-all.sh <triple>
#   2. XDYN_DEPS=<result> tools/deps/pack.sh <triple>
#   3. bump the tag, paste the lines below
#   4. gh release create <tag> build/scratch/deps-assets/lxdyn-deps-*.tar.zst
#
# Bump the tag whenever the recipes, the source pins, the zig version or the glibc floor
# change. Never re-upload under an existing tag: anyone who already fetched it keeps a
# closure these hashes no longer describe.
#
# These four came out of `nix build`, so each is the output of a derivation whose inputs are
# the recipes at this commit, the five sources pinned in flake.lock, and nothing else -- no
# network, no /usr, no host archiver. The closures-v0 assets predated that and predated the rename
# to target triples; both are why this is a new tag rather than an upload onto the old one.
#
# tag: closures-v2
6f6e04fae752ee4d055184a6a88c89d91c0ab04e9296fbde678c4787c67f9b13  lxdyn-deps-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.zst
f377a1fde59267910647d54a47fdff52d75df7249e02388779f9e1df96c25bb8  lxdyn-deps-x86_64-linux-musl.tar.zst
